<http://w3id.org/coresense/cso#SystemTrajectory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SysML constraint ConsistentWithSystem: states->ControlFunctions::forAll { in st : SystemState; st.entity == system }"@en .
<http://w3id.org/coresense/cso#SystemTrajectory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SysML constraint StateTimesUseIntervalTimeScale: states->ControlFunctions::forAll { in st : SystemState; st.timeInstant.mRef == timeInterval.initialTime.mRef }"@en .
<http://w3id.org/coresense/cso#SystemTrajectory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SysML constraint StateTimesWithinInterval: states->ControlFunctions::forAll { in st : SystemState; timeInterval.initialTime <= st.timeInstant and st.timeInstant <= timeInterval.finalTime }"@en .
<http://w3id.org/coresense/cso#SystemTrajectory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "SysML constraint StrictlyIncreasingTime: SequenceFunctions::size(states) == 1 or (1..(SequenceFunctions::size(states) - 1))->ControlFunctions::forAll { in i : Natural; states#(i).timeInstant < states#(i + 1).timeInstant }"@en .
<http://w3id.org/coresense/cso#SystemTrajectory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://w3id.org/coresense/cso> .
<http://w3id.org/coresense/cso#SystemTrajectory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "system trajectory"@en .
<http://w3id.org/coresense/cso#SystemTrajectory> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "SystemTrajectory"@en .
<http://w3id.org/coresense/cso#SystemTrajectory> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A trajectory is a time-ordered sequence of states representing one possible evolution of the system over a time interval."@en .
